Oh, and in first class you get a hot meal.
噢，而且头等舱还有热餐供应。

1149
00:48:25.260 --> 00:48:25.700
Ha!
哈！

1150
00:48:26.320 --> 00:48:27.940
Economy gets a sack lunch.
经济舱只有袋装午餐。

1151
00:48:28.340 --> 00:48:29.320
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1152
00:48:29.500 --> 00:48:30.640
Now you get nothing.
现在你什么也得不到了。

1153
00:48:30.900 --> 00:48:31.300
I know.
我知道。

1154
00:48:31.540 --> 00:48:34.660
I wonder if they upgraded me because I don't feel well.
我在想他们是不是因为我感觉不舒服才给我升的舱。

1155
00:48:34.820 --> 00:48:35.980
My cold is getting worse.
我的感冒越来越严重了。

1156
00:48:37.500 --> 00:48:38.620
How would they know?
他们怎么会知道？

1157
00:48:38.800 --> 00:48:40.160
Did you tell someone?
你跟谁说了吗？

1158
00:48:40.320 --> 00:48:41.800
I feel pretty sick.
我感觉病得很重。

1159
00:48:42.100 --> 00:48:44.840
My nose is driving me crazy and dripping a lot.
我的鼻子快把我折磨疯了，一直在流鼻涕。

1160
00:48:44.840 --> 00:48:47.320
Did you go to the airport and go, I'm so sorry to bother you.
你是不是去了机场，然后说，真抱歉打扰你了。

1161
00:48:47.420 --> 00:48:48.380
I don't feel well.
我感觉很不舒服。

1162
00:48:49.100 --> 00:48:51.860
Well, first class rocks, but I feel really sick.
好吧，头等舱是很棒，但我真的病得很重。

1163
00:48:52.060 --> 00:48:53.300
I might be getting the flu.
我可能要得流感了。

1164
00:48:54.340 --> 00:48:55.040
You know what?
你知道吗？

1165
00:48:55.120 --> 00:48:58.340
I want to see the journal entry of the person who sat next to you on this flight.
我真想看看坐在你旁边的那个人在飞行日志里写了什么。

1166
00:48:59.540 --> 00:49:05.560
My first time paying for first class and they seat me next to some sniffly, runny-nosed,
我第一次花钱坐头等舱，结果他们让我坐在一个吸鼻子、流鼻涕、

1167
00:49:06.220 --> 00:49:10.880
wide-eyed weirdo who's downing a drink pre-flight.
瞪大眼睛的怪人旁边，她还在起飞前猛灌饮料。

1168
00:49:11.120 --> 00:49:13.620
She keeps telling the flight attendants how sick she is.
她一直跟空乘说她病得有多重。

1169
00:49:14.040 --> 00:49:14.520
All right.
好吧。

1170
00:49:15.100 --> 00:49:16.980
The stewardess is the nicest lady.
空姐人真好。

1171
00:49:17.620 --> 00:49:19.540
She's really taking good care of me.
她真的把我照顾得很好。

1172
00:49:19.680 --> 00:49:21.520
I'm pretty sure now I have a fever.
我现在很确定我发烧了。

1173
00:49:21.760 --> 00:49:22.520
I'm getting worse.
我越来越严重了。

1174
00:49:22.760 --> 00:49:24.880
This is now two hours into the flight.
现在已经是飞行两个小时了。

1175
00:49:26.140 --> 00:49:27.040
Oh, goodness.
噢，天哪。

1176
00:49:27.540 --> 00:49:28.860
This is how it ends.
这就是结局了。

1177
00:49:29.420 --> 00:49:31.040
Feeling so sickly.
感觉病得好重。

1178
00:49:31.340 --> 00:49:32.320
Exclamation point.
感叹号。

1179
00:49:32.600 --> 00:49:33.200
Sad face.
悲伤的表情。

1180
00:49:33.540 --> 00:49:34.060
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

1181
00:49:35.160 --> 00:49:36.140
There you go.
给你。

1182
00:49:36.660 --> 00:49:37.940
Did you have the flu?
你当时得流感了吗？

1183
00:49:38.600 --> 00:49:39.960
Yeah, I got the flu.
是啊，我得了流感。

1184
00:49:40.320 --> 00:49:43.100
I showed up on Christmas Eve with the flu.
我平安夜那天带着流感出现了。

1185
00:49:44.200 --> 00:49:49.360
I like that it has callbacks like we've been, not like the other airport, as if we're going
我喜欢它有这种呼应，就像我们之前提到的，不是像另一个机场那样，好像我们

1186
00:49:49.360 --> 00:49:50.720
to be like, ah, I remember that entry.
会说，啊，我记得那篇日记。

1187
00:49:52.040 --> 00:49:56.920
Wait, I didn't count on this one, but here is January 2nd, 1997.
等等，我没算到这一篇，但这是1997年1月2日的。

1188
00:49:58.560 --> 00:50:00.560
Well, 1997 is here.
好吧，1997年到了。

1189
00:50:00.720 --> 00:50:01.860
Can you believe it?
你能相信吗？

1190
00:50:03.420 --> 00:50:05.740
You and the reader have been through so much.
你和读者一起经历了很多。

1191
00:50:07.180 --> 00:50:08.180
Oh, gosh.
噢，天哪。

1192
00:50:08.320 --> 00:50:08.580
All right.
好吧。

1193
00:50:08.680 --> 00:50:09.780
I'm going to stop for today.
我今天就写到这儿吧。

1194
00:50:10.120 --> 00:50:11.780
My journals are so embarrassing.
我的日记太尴尬了。

1195
00:50:12.340 --> 00:50:13.740
Thank you so much for that.
太感谢你了。

1196
00:50:13.960 --> 00:50:15.460
Well, that was delightful, Angela.
嗯，这真是太令人愉快了，安吉拉。

1197
00:50:15.780 --> 00:50:22.500
And I just want to say we do also have the option of a spinoff podcast called Angela's Journal.
我只想说，我们还有一个选择，就是做一个叫《安吉拉日记》的衍生播客。

1198
00:50:22.600 --> 00:50:23.020
No, no.
不，不。

1199
00:50:23.240 --> 00:50:24.180
We can't take it.
我们不能接受。

1200
00:50:24.180 --> 00:50:27.520
I'm just saying as we figure out what's next.
我只是在说，当我们考虑下一步该做什么的时候。

1201
00:50:27.520 --> 00:50:30.080
You can break down a journal entry each episode.
你可以把每一集的日记内容拆解开来。

1202
00:50:30.580 --> 00:50:31.820
Deep dives on it.
深入剖析一下。

1203
00:50:32.920 --> 00:50:35.080
I mean, who am I writing to?
我是说，我到底是在写给谁看呢？

1204
00:50:35.260 --> 00:50:36.460
Always is the question.
这永远是个问题。

1205
00:50:37.000 --> 00:50:37.340
Okay.
好吧。

1206
00:50:37.880 --> 00:50:39.860
I'm sorry you were sick that Christmas.
很遗憾那个圣诞节你生病了。

1207
00:50:40.380 --> 00:50:41.060
I know.
我知道。

1208
00:50:41.200 --> 00:50:42.060
That really stinks.
那真的很糟糕。

1209
00:50:42.320 --> 00:50:44.280
But I did get to fly first class.
但我确实坐了头等舱。

1210
00:50:44.540 --> 00:50:45.100
You did?
真的吗？

1211
00:50:45.300 --> 00:50:45.460
Yeah.
是的。

1212
00:50:46.120 --> 00:50:49.580
The bus is on the road and Toby has made it inside the church.
巴士在路上行驶，托比已经进了教堂。

1213
00:50:49.760 --> 00:50:50.240
Finally.
终于。

1214
00:50:50.740 --> 00:50:52.740
And we had a fan catch from Sean L.
我们还收到了一位粉丝肖恩·L的来信。

1215
00:50:52.860 --> 00:50:53.280
in Indiana.
来自印第安纳州。

1216
00:50:53.480 --> 00:50:54.080
It's wonderful.
太棒了。

1217
00:50:55.260 --> 00:50:58.940
Sean said, this is not a question, but something fun to look out for.
肖恩说，这不是个问题，但有个有趣的细节值得留意。

1218
00:50:59.180 --> 00:51:03.620
When Toby enters the church toward the end of the episode, you can see Dwight put his business
当托比在剧集快结束时走进教堂，你可以看到德怀特把他的名片

1219
00:51:03.620 --> 00:51:06.620
cards inside of the Bibles in the pews.
塞进了长椅上的圣经里。

1220
00:51:06.820 --> 00:51:07.380
Oh, Sean.
噢，肖恩。

1221
00:51:07.560 --> 00:51:09.060
This is something I was about to bring up.
这正是我打算提到的事。

1222
00:51:09.340 --> 00:51:09.780
Yes.
没错。

1223
00:51:09.880 --> 00:51:11.680
It's at 15 minutes and 50 seconds.
就在15分50秒的时候。

1224
00:51:11.680 --> 00:51:14.820
You can see Dwight's little business card popping out of the Bible.
你可以看到德怀特的小名片从圣经里露了出来。

1225
00:51:14.820 --> 00:51:15.640
That's right.
没错。

1226
00:51:15.820 --> 00:51:21.540
In deleted scenes, there is a scene, if you go to the DVD, Dwight is stuffing all of the
在删减片段里，如果你去看DVD，会有一个场景，德怀特正在把他的名片

1227
00:51:21.540 --> 00:51:25.360
Bibles and hymnals in all the pews with his business card.
塞进所有长椅上的圣经和赞美诗集里。

1228
00:51:25.700 --> 00:51:26.300
Incredible.
难以置信。

1229
00:51:27.020 --> 00:51:27.900
Well, Jim is panicking.
吉姆当时很慌张。

1230
00:51:27.900 --> 00:51:29.400
He cannot find Cece.
他找不到西西了。

1231
00:51:30.440 --> 00:51:33.900
And someone says a little blonde lady took Cece.
有人说一个小金发女士带走了西西。

1232
00:51:34.800 --> 00:51:39.180
Yes, that little blonde lady is Pam's mother, but Jim doesn't know that.
是的，那个小金发女士是帕姆的妈妈，但吉姆不知道。

1233
00:51:39.440 --> 00:51:45.740
So just as Pam is entering with a tray of sub sandwiches, Jim screams, stop that woman.
所以就在帕姆端着一托盘三明治走进来时，吉姆大喊，拦住那个女人。

1234
00:51:46.100 --> 00:51:46.980
Stop her now.
现在就拦住她。

1235
00:51:47.180 --> 00:51:48.080
She stole my baby.
她偷了我的孩子。

1236
00:51:48.260 --> 00:51:56.220
Kevin grabs Angela and her big bag right as Pam is entering and they all collide and this
凯文在帕姆进门时抓住了安吉拉和她的大包，他们撞在了一起，

1237
00:51:56.220 --> 00:51:58.880
tray of sub sandwiches goes flying in the air.
那一托盘三明治飞到了半空中。

1238
00:51:59.400 --> 00:52:01.040
Jenna, this was like a stunt for us.
珍娜，这对我们来说就像是一场特技表演。

1239
00:52:01.180 --> 00:52:01.620
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

1240
00:52:01.620 --> 00:52:02.380
I do remember.
我记得。

1241
00:52:02.660 --> 00:52:03.640
They had to break it down.
他们必须把动作拆解开。

1242
00:52:03.780 --> 00:52:04.680
We had to time it out.
我们得算好时间。

1243
00:52:04.800 --> 00:52:06.560
Someone was cuing you on the outside.
外面有人在给你打手势。

1244
00:52:07.000 --> 00:52:10.040
Brian had to be in the right place and I did and you had to come in.
布莱恩得在正确的位置，我也得在，你还得走进来。

1245
00:52:10.240 --> 00:52:11.220
I'm not going to lie.
我不撒谎。

1246
00:52:11.340 --> 00:52:17.180
When I watched it, I thought my tray fumble was a little forced.
当我重看的时候，我觉得我弄掉托盘的样子有点刻意。

1247
00:52:17.660 --> 00:52:18.640
I don't know if you saw it.
不知道你有没有看出来。

1248
00:52:18.740 --> 00:52:21.500
I brought the two trays together almost like symbols.
我把两个托盘撞在一起，就像敲镲一样。

1249
00:52:21.820 --> 00:52:22.820
It looked like a cartoon.
看起来像动画片一样。

1250
00:52:23.040 --> 00:52:24.760
It looked like Looney Tunes.
看起来就像《乐一通》。

1251
00:52:25.240 --> 00:52:27.240
It looked like so crazy.
看起来太疯狂了。

1252
00:52:27.860 --> 00:52:30.780
And I also wanted to know, why the silver platter?
而且我还想知道，为什么要用银盘？

1253
00:52:30.780 --> 00:52:31.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

1254
00:52:32.160 --> 00:52:34.280
She would be bringing them in in bags.
她本来是用袋子装进来的。

1255
00:52:34.500 --> 00:52:37.520
This whole silver platter thing was so over the top.
这整个银盘的事儿也太夸张了。

1256
00:52:37.700 --> 00:52:40.160
Well, we got a fan question from Kirsten W.
好吧，我们收到了一位粉丝Kirsten W.的提问，

1257
00:52:40.380 --> 00:52:42.200
in Fort Myers, Florida, who said,
她来自佛罗里达州的迈尔斯堡，她说，

1258
00:52:42.360 --> 00:52:47.020
when Pam comes back from getting the subs, she drops them when Angela bumps into her.
当帕姆买完三明治回来时，安吉拉撞到了她，三明治就掉了。

1259
00:52:47.320 --> 00:52:52.020
And then they insinuate that they can't eat the subs because they fell on the ground.
然后她们暗示说三明治掉在地上了就不能吃了。

1260
00:52:52.020 --> 00:52:53.500
But all the subs were wrapped.
但所有的三明治都是包好的。

1261
00:52:53.660 --> 00:52:55.640
So why couldn't they just pick them up and eat them?
所以为什么她们不能直接捡起来吃呢？

1262
00:52:56.080 --> 00:52:56.920
I agree.
我同意。

1263
00:52:57.180 --> 00:52:59.020
Yeah, I thought the same thing at firSt.
是啊，我起初也这么想。

1264
00:52:59.140 --> 00:53:05.820
But then I remembered that we were implying in our blocking that we were like stomping on them.
但后来我记起来，我们在走位时暗示过我们好像踩到了它们。

1265
00:53:05.960 --> 00:53:07.680
That like when they were on the ground.
就是当它们掉在地上的时候。

1266
00:53:07.920 --> 00:53:09.840
They got tripped on and stepped on.
它们被绊到又被踩到了。

1267
00:53:10.040 --> 00:53:10.220
Yeah.
没错。

1268
00:53:10.660 --> 00:53:13.800
Because of the whole struggle with Kevin and Angela and the purse and the scones.
因为凯文和安吉拉为了那个钱包和司康饼纠缠在一起。

1269
00:53:14.060 --> 00:53:15.120
That was the idea.
当时是这么设定的。

1270
00:53:15.280 --> 00:53:18.100
But like I said, I'm not sure we sold the moment.
但就像我说的，我不确定我们是否演出了那种效果。

1271
00:53:18.240 --> 00:53:18.700
Yeah, exactly.
是啊，确实。

1272
00:53:18.700 --> 00:53:20.320
As well as we could have.
没能达到我们预期的效果。

1273
00:53:20.520 --> 00:53:22.400
I want to tell you who is selling the moment.
我想告诉你们谁演出了效果。

1274
00:53:22.780 --> 00:53:29.540
There is a background actor behind Angela and Kevin while they're struggling with Angela's purse and the scones and all of that.
在安吉拉和凯文为了钱包和司康饼纠缠时，他们身后有个群演。

1275
00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:31.620
He gave me life.
他给了我很多灵感。

1276
00:53:31.780 --> 00:53:34.440
He is so horrified by this behavior.
他对这种行为感到非常震惊。

1277
00:53:34.600 --> 00:53:35.300
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

1278
00:53:35.300 --> 00:53:36.620
I wish I could see this.
真希望我也能看到这一幕。

1279
00:53:36.620 --> 00:53:37.660
It's so good.
太精彩了。

1280
00:53:38.420 --> 00:53:40.900
And I was like so tickled by it.
我当时被他逗乐了。

1281
00:53:41.140 --> 00:53:44.640
Well, Kevin's going to go through Angela's bag thinking he's going to find a baby.
好吧，凯文去翻安吉拉的包，以为能找到个婴儿。

1282
00:53:44.640 --> 00:53:49.640
But what he does find is thousands of scones in Angela's bag.
但他发现安吉拉的包里有成千上万个司康饼。

1283
00:53:49.860 --> 00:53:50.340
Thousands.
成千上万个。

1284
00:53:50.600 --> 00:53:52.060
All the scones, basically.
基本上所有的司康饼都在那儿。

1285
00:53:52.380 --> 00:53:54.980
Sconesy cider is not happy.
司康饼达人可不高兴了。

1286
00:53:55.500 --> 00:53:57.240
Angela's the new sconesy cider.
安吉拉成了新的司康饼达人。

1287
00:53:57.860 --> 00:54:01.380
We got mail about this scone theft.
我们收到了关于这次司康饼失窃事件的来信。

1288
00:54:01.680 --> 00:54:02.220
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

1289
00:54:02.460 --> 00:54:02.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1290
00:54:03.140 --> 00:54:03.760
Sarah M.
莎拉·M.

1291
00:54:03.880 --> 00:54:05.360
from Harrisburg, Pennsylvania said,
来自宾夕法尼亚州的哈里斯堡，她说，

1292
00:54:05.440 --> 00:54:07.840
I never understood why Angela took all the scones.
我一直不明白安吉拉为什么要拿走所有的司康饼。

1293
00:54:08.140 --> 00:54:11.300
Did she do it to sabotage the christening luncheon?
她是想破坏洗礼午宴吗？

1294
00:54:11.300 --> 00:54:13.480
And then Susanna H.
然后苏珊娜·H.

1295
00:54:13.880 --> 00:54:15.880
from Clermont, Florida said,
来自佛罗里达州的克莱蒙特说，

1296
00:54:16.000 --> 00:54:16.560
Hot take.
大胆猜测一下。

1297
00:54:16.680 --> 00:54:20.740
I think Angela stole the scones to make Pam and Jim look even worse for having so little food.
我觉得安吉拉偷走司康饼是为了让帕姆和吉姆看起来更糟糕，因为他们准备的食物太少了。

1298
00:54:20.900 --> 00:54:22.520
I don't think she even likes scones.
我觉得她甚至都不喜欢吃司康饼。

1299
00:54:23.560 --> 00:54:24.760
Angela, what's your take?
安吉拉，你怎么看？

1300
00:54:24.980 --> 00:54:26.000
Strong words.
话说的很重啊。

1301
00:54:26.160 --> 00:54:26.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1302
00:54:26.940 --> 00:54:27.300
Well?
怎么样？

1303
00:54:27.580 --> 00:54:28.560
Are you a saboteur?
你是破坏分子吗？

1304
00:54:28.740 --> 00:54:30.420
I don't think she's a saboteur.
我觉得她不是破坏分子。

1305
00:54:30.960 --> 00:54:38.120
I think she might just be that person that takes extra rolls when they leave a party or a few extra party favors.
我觉得她可能只是那种离开派对时会多拿几卷纸巾，或者多拿几个派对小礼物的人。

1306
00:54:38.120 --> 00:54:41.760
Or if you have fruit set out, she might take some of your bananas and apples.
或者如果你摆了水果，她可能会拿走你的一些香蕉和苹果。

1307
00:54:42.420 --> 00:54:44.120
I think she might be that person.
我觉得她可能是那种人。

1308
00:54:44.420 --> 00:54:47.180
Well, before we're done closing out this reception,
好吧，在我们结束这次招待会之前，

1309
00:54:47.560 --> 00:54:51.060
there was a deleted scene I'd like to talk about that happened at the reception.
我想聊聊一个在招待会上发生的被删减片段。

1310
00:54:51.340 --> 00:54:54.000
It was sort of the end of the day, and a lot of people had left,
当时差不多是这一天的尾声了，很多人都已经离开了，

1311
00:54:54.080 --> 00:54:57.920
and Jim and Pam finally got the small, intimate gathering they were hoping for.
吉姆和帕姆终于得到了他们所期待的那种小型、亲密的聚会。

1312
00:54:58.200 --> 00:55:00.620
And Jim gives a really sweet speech.
吉姆发表了一段非常感人的演讲。

1313
00:55:00.900 --> 00:55:02.000
I thought we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

1314
00:55:05.020 --> 00:55:06.060
We're going to have your attention.
请大家注意一下。

1315
00:55:06.600 --> 00:55:09.740
Today, we christened our daughter, Cecilia Marie.
今天，我们为女儿塞西莉亚·玛丽举行了洗礼。

1316
00:55:10.660 --> 00:55:13.760
And, yeah, for a moment there, I thought she was bailing on her own reception,
而且，是的，有一瞬间我以为她要逃离自己的招待会了，

1317
00:55:13.840 --> 00:55:16.600
but I guess she decided to stick it out.
但我猜她还是决定坚持到底。

1318
00:55:16.860 --> 00:55:21.840
We named Cece after Pam's grandmother, Cecilia, and after my grandmother, Marie.
我们给西西取名是为了纪念帕姆的祖母塞西莉亚，以及我的祖母玛丽。

1319
00:55:22.820 --> 00:55:25.980
And I always remember how cool Marie was.
我一直记得玛丽有多酷。

1320
00:55:26.280 --> 00:55:29.980
She loved people, and she loved a full and crazy house.
她热爱人群，也喜欢家里热热闹闹、乱成一团的样子。

1321
00:55:30.660 --> 00:55:34.080
And nothing ever rattled her, so she would have loved it here today.
而且没什么事能让她心烦意乱，所以她一定会喜欢今天这里的场景。

1322
00:55:34.880 --> 00:55:37.680
And we just hope that Cece has that same carefree spirit.
我们只希望西西也能拥有同样无忧无虑的精神。

1323
00:55:38.820 --> 00:55:42.040
Thank you guys all for coming and sharing this special day with us.
谢谢大家前来与我们分享这个特别的日子。

1324
00:55:50.350 --> 00:55:52.670
Who wants to go pick up Michael and Andy?
谁想去接迈克尔和安迪？

1325
00:55:55.460 --> 00:55:59.260
Okay, so that's how that really sweet speech ends.
好了，那段非常感人的演讲就是这样结束的。

1326
00:55:59.480 --> 00:56:02.280
And when Pam says, who wants to go pick up Michael and Andy,
当帕姆说“谁想去接迈克尔和安迪”时，

1327
00:56:02.820 --> 00:56:08.420
Erin flies out of her seat, doesn't say anything to Gabe or anyone, and sprints out the door.
艾琳从座位上弹了起来，没跟盖博或任何人打招呼，就冲出了门外。

1328
00:56:09.020 --> 00:56:09.500
Wow.
哇。

1329
00:56:09.880 --> 00:56:10.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1330
00:56:11.060 --> 00:56:11.340
Hmm.
嗯。

1331
00:56:11.820 --> 00:56:13.240
But wasn't that a sweet speech?
不过那段演讲很感人，不是吗？

1332
00:56:13.400 --> 00:56:14.240
That was really sweet.
真的很感人。

1333
00:56:14.400 --> 00:56:17.040
And we found out sort of inspiration for the baby's name.
而且我们了解到了宝宝名字的灵感来源。

1334
00:56:17.160 --> 00:56:17.740
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1335
00:56:19.380 --> 00:56:26.520
Well, I guess we should go to the bus because Michael and Andy are regretting their decision.
好吧，我想我们该去巴士那边了，因为迈克尔和安迪正在后悔他们的决定。

1336
00:56:27.140 --> 00:56:30.340
It's going to take two days to get there.
到那儿需要两天时间。

1337
00:56:30.580 --> 00:56:32.200
Their next stop is Tennessee.
他们的下一站是田纳西州。

1338
00:56:33.160 --> 00:56:36.340
Yeah, Michael and Andy went off the bus.
是的，迈克尔和安迪下了巴士。

1339
00:56:36.520 --> 00:56:38.020
They're changing their minds.
他们改变主意了。

1340
00:56:38.200 --> 00:56:38.920
Full stop.
彻底改变了。

1341
00:56:39.080 --> 00:56:42.640
And they asked the bus driver to stop the bus.
他们要求巴士司机停车。

1342
00:56:42.820 --> 00:56:44.660
The bus driver was played by Terry James.
巴士司机由特里·詹姆斯饰演。

1343
00:56:45.260 --> 00:56:49.920
You know, Randy said that Allison Jones read stunt drivers for this role.
你知道，兰迪说艾莉森·琼斯为这个角色面试了特技司机。

1344
00:56:49.920 --> 00:56:55.380
They had to hold a certain category license because he was really hoping that the person
他们必须持有特定类别的驾照，因为他真的很希望选中的演员

1345
00:56:55.380 --> 00:56:58.220
they cast as this actor could actually drive the bus.
能够真正驾驶那辆巴士。

1346
00:56:58.680 --> 00:57:02.180
So our stunt coordinator, Wally Crowder, suggested Terry James.
所以我们的特技协调员沃利·克劳德推荐了特里·詹姆斯。

1347
00:57:02.300 --> 00:57:03.020
He read for the role.
他试镜了这个角色。

1348
00:57:03.160 --> 00:57:03.940
He did great.
他表现得很棒。

1349
00:57:04.040 --> 00:57:06.560
And he could really drive during this scene.
而且他在拍摄这场戏时真的能驾驶巴士。

1350
00:57:06.900 --> 00:57:08.520
I thought Terry did so great.
我觉得特里表现得太棒了。

1351
00:57:08.640 --> 00:57:11.020
I loved it when he said, you shouldn't talk to a bus driver.
我很喜欢他说的那句，你不该跟公交车司机搭话。

1352
00:57:12.880 --> 00:57:13.360
Yes.
没错。

1353
00:57:13.620 --> 00:57:15.000
Well, they start making a scene.
嗯，他们开始闹事了。

1354
00:57:15.140 --> 00:57:17.240
They're screaming, stop the bus.
他们尖叫着，停车，停车。

1355
00:57:17.380 --> 00:57:18.080
Stop the bus.
停车。

1356
00:57:18.080 --> 00:57:21.360
Andy is, I mean, he's like starting to cry.
安迪，我是说，他都快哭出来了。

1357
00:57:21.920 --> 00:57:26.040
And the young kids that are on the bus are like, what's going on, you guys?
车上的小孩子们都在问，你们怎么了？

1358
00:57:26.060 --> 00:57:26.720
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

1359
00:57:27.060 --> 00:57:29.960
Yeah, the female student was played by Erica Murr.
没错，那个女学生是由埃里卡·穆尔饰演的。

1360
00:57:30.080 --> 00:57:36.180
And then the other gentleman, the kind of scraggly-haired fella, we got some mail about him.
还有另一位男士，就是那个头发乱糟糟的家伙，我们收到了一些关于他的来信。

1361
00:57:36.380 --> 00:57:38.160
And that led me down a road.
这让我深入挖掘了一番。

1362
00:57:38.740 --> 00:57:41.240
Zian from Amarillo, Texas said,
来自德克萨斯州阿马里洛的齐安说，

1363
00:57:41.380 --> 00:57:44.460
My brother-in-law had a small guest spot in this episode.
我姐夫在这集里有个小客串。

1364
00:57:44.460 --> 00:57:46.340
His name is Seth Allison.
他叫塞斯·艾利森。

1365
00:57:46.340 --> 00:57:50.320
He is the youth group kid with the scraggly hair that says,
他就是那个留着乱发、说这句台词的青年团成员，

1366
00:57:50.740 --> 00:57:51.940
Are you coming with us?
你们要跟我们一起去吗？

1367
00:57:52.040 --> 00:57:53.460
And stop the dang bus.
还有那句，快让该死的车停下。

1368
00:57:53.940 --> 00:57:56.320
He is still in Hollywood working in comedy.
他现在还在好莱坞从事喜剧工作。

1369
00:57:56.640 --> 00:58:00.240
In fact, he was on an episode of the gong show that Ed Helms judged.
事实上，他上过一期艾德·赫尔姆斯担任评委的《铜锣秀》。

1370
00:58:00.580 --> 00:58:08.660
He has also been on America's Got Talent several times and traveled to other countries to be on their versions of the show.
他还多次参加过《美国达人秀》，并去其他国家参加过当地版本的节目。

1371
00:58:08.660 --> 00:58:11.740
His stage name is Sethward.
他的艺名是塞斯沃德。

1372
00:58:12.180 --> 00:58:13.000
Angela?
安吉拉？

1373
00:58:13.580 --> 00:58:14.400
Sethward?
塞斯沃德？

1374
00:58:14.580 --> 00:58:14.980
Yeah?
怎么了？

1375
00:58:15.180 --> 00:58:20.640
Has appeared on 12 episodes of America's Got Talent over multiple seasons.
他在多季《美国达人秀》中出场过12次。

1376
00:58:20.800 --> 00:58:21.300
Wow.
哇。

1377
00:58:21.540 --> 00:58:23.200
Five episodes of the gong show.
五集《铜锣秀》。

1378
00:58:23.200 --> 00:58:39.400
He always appears as a type of animal who, I don't know how to explain it, but he has been Sethward the worm, Sethward the phoenix, Sethward the peacock, Sethward the walrus,
他总是扮演某种动物，我不知道该怎么解释，但他演过毛毛虫塞斯沃德、凤凰塞斯沃德、孔雀塞斯沃德、海象塞斯沃德，

1379
00:58:39.680 --> 00:58:43.560
the caterpillar, the snake, the chicken, the cow, and the bunny.
还有毛毛虫、蛇、鸡、牛和兔子。

1380
00:58:43.560 --> 00:58:45.820
What does he do when he's an animal?
他扮演动物时会做什么？

1381
00:58:46.260 --> 00:58:48.180
Well, it's very interesting.
嗯，这很有意思。

1382
00:58:48.520 --> 00:58:52.040
So, the first one that I saw was Sethward the caterpillar.
我看到的第一个是毛毛虫塞斯沃德。

1383
00:58:52.220 --> 00:58:52.580
Okay.
好的。

1384
00:58:52.580 --> 00:58:59.960
He is in a caterpillar outfit, and when he comes out onto the stage, he falls down.
他穿着毛毛虫的服装，一上台就摔倒了。

1385
00:59:00.280 --> 00:59:10.280
He rolls off the stage, and then he goes up on the stage, and he goes through a metamorphosis and turns into a butterfly, but they didn't let him finish.
他从舞台上滚了下去，然后又爬上台，经历了一场蜕变，变成了蝴蝶，但他们没让他演完。

1386
00:59:10.280 --> 00:59:11.620
They judged him out.
评委把他淘汰了。

1387
00:59:11.740 --> 00:59:12.140
Oh.
噢。

1388
00:59:12.140 --> 00:59:18.900
But he became sort of like an audience favorite, so he came back multiple times.
但他成了观众的最爱，所以他多次回归。

1389
00:59:19.240 --> 00:59:23.240
Finally, they let him move forward, but he was just a recurring.
最后，他们让他晋级了，但他只是个常驻嘉宾。

1390
00:59:23.580 --> 00:59:25.940
Like a recurring fan favorite of the show.
就像是节目里常驻的粉丝宠儿。

1391
00:59:26.060 --> 00:59:30.080
Yes, of America's Got Talent coming back in different forms every time.
是的，每次都以不同的形象回归《美国达人秀》。

1392
00:59:30.320 --> 00:59:31.880
I went down a rabbit hole.
我陷入了深挖的漩涡。

1393
00:59:32.120 --> 00:59:33.880
I watched all of his appearances.
我看了他所有的表演。

1394
00:59:34.480 --> 00:59:36.180
Is it lots of, like, physical comedy?
是那种有很多肢体喜剧的表演吗？

1395
00:59:36.420 --> 00:59:36.900
Yes.
是的。

1396
00:59:37.120 --> 00:59:37.620
Yes.
没错。

1397
00:59:37.860 --> 00:59:40.100
But also just very charming and funny.
但同时也非常迷人且有趣。

1398
00:59:40.320 --> 00:59:42.000
I'll have to check it out, Sethward.
我得去看看，塞斯沃德。

1399
00:59:42.140 --> 00:59:49.020
Well, they finally stopped the bus and let them off, and we see that they call someone to come get them, and it is Erin.
好吧，他们最终停下车让他们下了车，我们看到他们打电话叫人来接，来的人是艾琳。

1400
00:59:49.600 --> 00:59:52.620
Yes, and another student gets off the bus with them, too.
是的，还有另一名学生也和他们一起下了车。

1401
00:59:52.860 --> 00:59:53.720
Yes, that's right.
没错，就是这样。

1402
00:59:54.120 --> 00:59:55.780
He's like, don't tell my parents.
他当时说，别告诉我父母。

1403
00:59:56.680 --> 00:59:59.380
That student was played by Jeff Loveness.
那个学生是由杰夫·洛文尼斯扮演的。

1404
00:59:59.520 --> 01:00:00.420
He's a writer-performer.
他是一位编剧兼演员。

1405
01:00:00.520 --> 01:00:07.860
He's worked on Rick and Morty, the Onion News Network, and has been a writer for the Emmys and Oscar televised prograMs.
他曾参与过《瑞克和莫蒂》和《洋葱新闻网》的制作，还担任过艾美奖和奥斯卡颁奖典礼的电视节目编剧。

1406
01:00:08.300 --> 01:00:11.140
We got some fan mail from Alania D.
我们收到了来自威斯康星州阿拉尼亚·D的粉丝来信，

1407
01:00:11.400 --> 01:00:13.040
in Wisconsin and Lauren H.
还有加利福尼亚州圣克拉里塔的劳伦·H，

1408
01:00:13.120 --> 01:00:18.440
in Santa Clarita, California, who both pointed out that he looks a lot like Steve Carell.
她们都指出他长得很像史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

1409
01:00:18.440 --> 01:00:22.240
They thought he looked like Steve's teenage doppelganger.
她们觉得他看起来就像史蒂夫的少年版替身。

1410
01:00:22.460 --> 01:00:25.420
They wanted to know if he was related to Steve, but he's not.
她们想知道他是否和史蒂夫有亲戚关系，但其实并没有。

1411
01:00:25.540 --> 01:00:26.200
Oh, no, no, he's not.
哦，不，不，他没有。

1412
01:00:26.300 --> 01:00:27.760
I can kind of see it.
我确实能看出一点相似之处。

1413
01:00:28.320 --> 01:00:32.280
Well, they're going to get in with Erin, and Michael wants to know, is the reception still going on?
好吧，他们要去找艾琳了，迈克尔想知道，招待会还在进行吗？

1414
01:00:32.340 --> 01:00:33.920
And she said, no, most everyone left.
她说，没有，大部分人都走了。

1415
01:00:34.000 --> 01:00:35.640
In fact, I think they all went to see a movie.
事实上，我想他们都去看电影了。

1416
01:00:36.280 --> 01:00:37.600
And Michael got what he wanted.
迈克尔得到了他想要的。

1417
01:00:37.900 --> 01:00:38.720
Everyone's hanging out.
大家都聚在一起。

1418
01:00:38.720 --> 01:00:42.920
Well, they're having a memory together, and he's very happy to be back in this country.
好吧，他们正在共同创造一段回忆，他很高兴能回到这个国家。

1419
01:00:43.800 --> 01:00:45.760
Yes, the country he never left.
没错，他从未离开过的国家。

1420
01:00:45.900 --> 01:00:46.320
That's right.
就是这样。

1421
01:00:47.120 --> 01:00:49.580
Well, that was Christening, everybody.
好了，各位，以上就是《洗礼》这一集的内容。

1422
01:00:49.940 --> 01:00:53.660
Thank you so much to Randy Cordray for sharing behind-the-scenes details with us.
非常感谢兰迪·科德雷与我们分享幕后细节。

1423
